## Configs

`configs/defaults/run.yaml` lists every setting with its default, commented where the options or meaning are not
obvious. It is generated from the schema in `src/{{ package }}/config.py`, so it is never edited.
{% if example %}
`configs/signal/` holds one generated file per signal kind; `signal=<kind>` picks one.
{% endif %}
To change a value:

| for | edit |
|---|---|
| one run | `key=value` on the command line; the run directory records it |
{% if example %}
| a reusable variant of one part | a preset you add to its group, such as `configs/signal/noisy.yaml` below |
{% endif %}
| every run of this repo | `configs/run.yaml`, the entry config, below its `defaults:` list |
| the default itself | the schema, then `make configs` |
{% if example %}

A preset starts from a kind and changes some of its values. This one is selected with `signal=noisy`:

```yaml
# configs/signal/noisy.yaml
defaults:
  - gaussian

std: 3.0
```
{% endif %}

Secrets go in `.env`, reach configs as `${oc.env:NAME,null}` and are typed `SecretStr` in the schema: only those
fields are masked in a run's `config.yaml`.
